-- title:
--   Ends and smooth-point stalks on the supersingular chart, q=3
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$ subject to $q = 3$, a nonzero $M'$ with $q \nmid M'$, and an auxiliary prime $\ell_g$ with $\ell_g \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ and $\ell_g \mid M'$. Write $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ for `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` and $F =$ `fieldBar q M'` for the intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb Q}((T))$ obtained as `laurentBaseChange` of the function field of $X_H$ of level $q^2M'$, where $H =$ `levelH q M'` is the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb Z/q)^\times$, i.e. the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$; here a `Place K F` is a valuation subring of $F$ containing the image of $K$, distinct from $F$ and a principal ideal ring, with `ord` the associated normalised integer valuation, `IsRational` meaning that $K$ surjects onto its residue field, and `evalAt` the $K$-valued evaluation of an element of the valuation subring (and $0$ off it).
--
--   The base data are: a valuation subring $A \subseteq \overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $q$ a non-unit of $A$ (`LiesOverPrime`); a finite set $W$ of places of `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` over $\kappa =$ `ResidueField A` whose members are exactly the elements of `ssPlaces q M' (ResidueField A)`, that is the places $w$ that are rational, satisfy `IsAffineGeomPlace`, and have $w.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of the generator `jGeomGen` lying in `ssJSet q (ResidueField A)`; the inequality $hle$ of intermediate fields `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` $\le F$; a chosen $s \in W$; an intermediate field $k_0$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$ together with $\pi_0 \in k_0$ lying in $A$; the hypotheses that $A \cap k_0$ (formally `A.comap` along $k_0 \hookrightarrow \overline{\mathbb Q}$) is a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$, is henselian, and has algebraically closed residue field; the approximation hypothesis $h\kappa$ that every $a \in A$ differs from some element of $k_0 \cap A$ by an element of the maximal ideal of $A$; the hypothesis that $\kappa$ is algebraically closed; an algebra structure of `GaloisField q 2` on $\kappa$, the hypothesis that [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q κ`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) (the quotient of $\kappa[X_0,X_1]$ by `drinfeldPoly q κ - 1`) is a domain, and an index $\zeta_{ix} \in$ `Idx q`, the set of primitive $q$-th roots of unity in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$. Finally there are an intermediate field $K_b$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/k_0$ with $K_b = \bot$, a valuation subring $A_b \subseteq K_b$ whose elements are exactly those lying in $A$, the hypotheses that $A_b$ is a henselian discrete valuation ring, and a uniformiser $\varpi_b \ne 0$ generating the maximal ideal of $A_b$.
--
--   The conclusion is stated for $F$ viewed as a $k_0$-algebra through $k_0 \hookrightarrow \overline{\mathbb Q} \to F$, and asserts the following for every intermediate field $F_0$ of $F/k_0$ and every valuation subring $W_0 \subseteq F_0$ subject to the five conditions: (G1) $\overline{\mathbb Q} \cdot F_0 = F$, i.e. the join of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ is $\top$; (G2) for $x \in k_0$, $x \in A$ if and only if the image of $x$ in $F_0$ lies in $W_0$; (G3) $W_0$ is a discrete valuation ring; (G4) the image of $\pi_0$ lies in $W_0$ and generates its maximal ideal; (G5) the linear-disjointness condition: for every finite extension $K'$ of $k_0$ inside $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, every $m$, every $c : \mathrm{Fin}\,m \to \overline{\mathbb Q}$ and every $a : \mathrm{Fin}\,m \to F$ with all $a_i$ in the join of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $K'$, if $c$ is $K'$-linearly independent and $\sum_i \iota(c_i)\,a_i = 0$ then all $a_i = 0$.
--
--   Furthermore, for every subring $B \subseteq F$ with an $A_b$-algebra structure $\mathrm{alg}$ satisfying the chart conditions (C1) the structure map $A_b \to B$ is compatible with the inclusions $A_b \subseteq K_b \subseteq \overline{\mathbb Q} \to F$; (C2) $B$ is contained in the join $E$ of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $K_b$; (C3) every element of $E$ is a ratio $g/h$ with $g, h \in B$, $h \ne 0$; (C4) $B$ is formally smooth over $A_b$; (C5) $B$ is of finite presentation over $A_b$; (C6) $B/\varpi_b B$ has Krull dimension at most $1$; (C7) every element of $B$ lies in $F_0$ and in $W_0$; (C8) the image of $\varpi_b$ is a prime element of $B$; (C9) $W_0$ is the localisation of $B$ at that prime, in the sense that $f \in F_0$ lies in $W_0$ exactly when $f h = g$ for some $g, h \in B$ with the image of $\varpi_b$ not dividing $h$; (C10) the image in $F$, via the inclusion $hle$, of the element `coeffEmb (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) jq` of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` — the $q$-expansion of $j$ — lies in $B$; (C11) $B$ is stable under `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` for every $\zeta \in$ `Idx q` and every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$; and (C12) the special-fibre identification: for every algebra structure of `GaloisField q 2` on $\kappa$, every proof that `CoordRing q κ` is a domain and every $\zeta \in$ `Idx q`, there exist a subgroup $C_s$ of the $(q+1)$-st roots of unity of `GaloisField q 2` and a ring homomorphism $\rho : B \to$ [`DrinfeldCurve.quotField q κ Cs`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelSemistableCoveringW2.html#L32) (the fixed field, inside the fraction field of `CoordRing q κ`, of the subgroup generated by the `hFunctionFieldAction` of the elements $(1,\zeta')$ for $\zeta' \in C_s$) such that $\#C_s = 2\,\cdot$`placeWidthChar q M' s`, $\ker \rho$ is generated by the image of $\varpi_b$, $\rho$ composed with $A_b \to B$ is the residue map $A \to \kappa$ followed by $\kappa \to$ `quotField`, every element of `quotField` is a ratio $\rho(g)/\rho(h)$ with $g,h \in B$, the image of $\rho$ consists exactly of those elements of `quotField` whose image in the Drinfeld function field lies in the image of `CoordRing q κ`, and $\rho$ is equivariant: for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ with $(\mathrm{redQ}_q\gamma, 1) \in$ `hSubgroup q` and $f \in B$ with `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ⁻¹` $f \in B$, one has $\rho(\,$`levelAutBar q M' ζ γ⁻¹`$\,f) =$ `hFunctionFieldAction q κ` of $(\mathrm{redQ}_q\gamma,1)$ applied to $\rho(f)$, computed in the Drinfeld function field.
--
--   Finally, for every field $FSS$ that is a $\kappa$-algebra, every regular prolongation $R$ of $A$ to $F$ with residue field $FSS$ — that is, a valuation subring $R.\mathrm{integers}$ of $F$ meeting $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ exactly in $A$, together with a surjection $R.\mathrm{residue} : R.\mathrm{integers} \to FSS$ whose kernel is the maximal ideal, compatible with $A \to \kappa$, and such that every nonzero $f \in F$ admits a scalar $c$ with $c f$ integral of nonzero residue — and subject to the compatibility that for $f \in F_0$ one has $f \in R.\mathrm{integers}$ if and only if $f \in W_0$, there exist a finite set $N$ of places of $FSS$ over $\kappa$, a family of subrings $S_Q \subseteq F$, ring homomorphisms $\varphi_Q : A_b[T] \to S_Q$, ring homomorphisms $\chi_Q : S_Q \to \kappa$ and sets $D_Q$ of places of $F$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, indexed by the places $Q$ of $FSS$ over $\kappa$, such that:
--
--   (a) $\#N = q + 1$;
--
--   (b) for every $Q \notin N$ the following twelve clauses hold: (i) the image in $F$ of every $a \in A_b$ lies in $S_Q$; (ii) $\varphi_Q(\mathrm{C}\,a)$ is that image, for every $a \in A_b$; (iii) $\chi_Q(\varphi_Q(\mathrm{C}\,a))$ is the residue of $a$ in $\kappa$; (iv) $\chi_Q(\varphi_Q(T)) = 0$; (v) $S_Q$ is local and $\ker \chi_Q$ is its maximal ideal; (vi) $S_Q$ is contained in the join $E$ of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $K_b$; (vii) every element of $E$ is a ratio of two elements of $S_Q$ with nonzero denominator; (viii) $\varphi_Q$ is formally smooth, formally unramified and essentially of finite type; (ix) $S_Q \subseteq R.\mathrm{integers}$, and an element of $S_Q$ lies in the maximal ideal of $R.\mathrm{integers}$ exactly when it is divisible in $S_Q$ by $\varphi_Q(\mathrm{C}\,\varpi_b)$; (x) every $f \in S_Q$ lies in $R.\mathrm{integers}$, its $R$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $Q$, and the residue at $Q$ of that element is the image of $\chi_Q(f)$ under $\kappa \to Q.\mathrm{ResidueField}$; (xi) $\varphi_Q(T)$ lies in $R.\mathrm{integers}$ and its $R$-residue has $Q$-order $1$; (xii) a place $P$ of $F$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ belongs to $D_Q$ if and only if $P$ is rational, every $f \in S_Q$ lies in the valuation subring of $P$ with $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f) \in A$, and for every $f \in S_Q$ the value $A.\mathrm{valuation}(P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f))$ is $< 1$ precisely when $\chi_Q(f) = 0$;
--
--   (c) the discs are pairwise disjoint: if $Q, Q' \notin N$ and some $P$ lies in both $D_Q$ and $D_{Q'}$, then $Q = Q'$;
--
--   (d) for $Q \notin N$ and $P \in D_Q$, the $P$-order of the image of $j$ in $F$ (the element of (C10)) is $\ge 0$;
--
--   (e) equivariance under the level automorphisms: for every $\tau$ in the subgroup of $\mathrm{Aut}_{\overline{\mathbb Q}}(F)$ generated by the automorphisms `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` with $\zeta \in$ `Idx q` and $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$, and every proof $h\tau$ that $\tau$ preserves $R.\mathrm{integers}$, the induced $\kappa$-automorphism `R.resAut τ hτ` of $FSS$ satisfies: $Q \in N$ if and only if its translate lies in $N$; and for $Q \notin N$ the translated disc [`AlgebraicCurve.RegularProlongation.smulDisc τ (D_Q)`](def/AlgebraicCurve_ResidueDiscs.html#L120), namely $\{P : \tau^{-1} \cdot P \in D_Q\}$, equals $D_{Q'}$ for $Q'$ the translate of $Q$ by `R.resAut τ hτ`.
--
--   Here `placeWidthChar q N w` is `jWidthChar q` of $w.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of `jGeomGen`, divided by `placeRamificationJ N w`; for $q = 3$ the numerator is $6$ when that value is $0$ and $1$ otherwise.
--
--   This is the $q = 3$ case, in the presence of an auxiliary prime $\ell_g \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ dividing $M'$, of the passage from an affine chart $B$ of the semistable model along a supersingular component to the geometry of that component: it produces the $q+1$ ends, and for each remaining place of the special fibre a local stalk with an étale coordinate, a residue character and the corresponding residue disc of places of the characteristic-zero function field, all compatibly with the $\Gamma_0(M')$-level automorphisms. It is used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_klevel_supersingularDVR_baseSmoothPointStalks_of_eq_three_of_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_klevel_supersingularDVR_baseSmoothPointStalks_of_eq_three_of_dvd), and assembles the chart-level results on the residue surjection, the ends, the smooth-point stalks and the residue discs.
